    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE GREAT LAKES WAVE HEIGHT</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-24 09:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source updated:</b> Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:26:26 GMT<br/><b>Source version:</b> glwu-20260925-0100Z<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-24 10:24 PM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_height/legend.png?v=glwu-20260925-0100Z" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Wave height (feet, one continuous gradient): <b>0</b> dark blue → <b>2</b> blue/cyan → <b>5</b> cyan/green → <b>9</b> green/yellow → <b>12–15</b> yellow-orange → orange → <b>20</b> red → <b>23–26</b> red-violet → violet → <b>30+</b> dark purple extreme. Model maximum this run: <b>4.1 ft</b>. Values above 30 ft stay dark purple. Significant height = average of highest third of waves.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III)<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260925/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t01z.grib2">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20260925/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t01z.grib2</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of temperature and ice layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
